rname>Clayman</surname><given-names>RV</given-names></name><name><surname>Ornstein</surname><given-names>DK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Robotic versus Standard Laparoscopic Partial/Wedge Nephrectomy: A Comparison of Intraoperative and Perioperative Results from a Single Institution</article-title><source>J Endourol</source><year>2008</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>947</fpage><lpage>952</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18397157</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1089/end.2007.0376</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aron</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Koenig</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaouk</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Nguyen</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Desai</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Gill</surname><given-names>IS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Robotic and laparoscopic partial nephrectomy: a matched-pair comparison from a high-volume centre</article-title><source>BJU Int</source><year>2008</year><volume>102</volume><fpage>86</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18336600</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1464-410X.2008.07580.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Blatt</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Linehan</surname><given-names>WM</given-names></name><name><surname>Pinto</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Robotic partial nephrectomy for complex renal tumors: surgical technique</article-title><source>Eur Urol</source><year>2008</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>514</fpage